WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.854
Equator Development Finance lends through
partner banks.

00:00:03.854 --> 00:00:09.485
Before it lends, it needs to know who owns
them, who runs them, and what their files

00:00:09.485 --> 00:00:10.490
actually prove.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:15.451
This is a partner-bank assessment, run on the
platform, on Equator's data.

00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:17.998
The data in this film is illustrative.

00:00:18.629 --> 00:00:21.905
Equator is onboarded as an evaluation
engagement.

00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:27.520
Its due diligence is approved by a second
person, its data is processed under a data

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.469
processing agreement, and the term and the
deletion date are set before any data arrives.

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:37.480
Our external-manager film walks through each
of those steps.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.184
Equator's compliance officer opens External
Diagnostics.

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:47.801
The assessment type is Equator's own
engagement, so the platform asks for exactly

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.564
four files:

00:00:48.564 --> 00:00:54.389
the banks, their owners and directors, the
evidence each supplied, and the debarment

00:00:54.389 --> 00:00:54.736
list.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.575
Four files load.

00:00:56.575 --> 00:01:02.522
Every row is validated, and anything that
fails is quarantined and counted, never

00:01:02.522 --> 00:01:03.109
dropped.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:09.253
The files are frozen in an immutable snapshot,
with a fingerprint, and run through the

00:01:09.253 --> 00:01:12.143
platform's own screening and evidence engines.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.522
One match.

00:01:13.522 --> 00:01:19.502
A director of Kilimanjaro Trust Bank, with no
shareholding at all, is on the multilateral

00:01:19.502 --> 00:01:21.988
debarment list, under a listed alias.

00:01:21.988 --> 00:01:26.087
A check of the shareholders alone would never
have found him.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.604
And what each file proves.

00:01:28.604 --> 00:01:30.408
Rift Valley, five of five.

00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:32.003
Lakeshore, two of five:

00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:38.039
its banking licence has expired, its anti-
money-laundering policy is not verified, its

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:43.451
ownership chart is missing, and a fifth of its
ownership is not accounted for.

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.607
Equator downloads its findings pack:

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:51.658
the report, the rows behind every table, and a
fingerprint for every file.

00:01:51.658 --> 00:01:55.685
Commercial records delivery against the pack's
fingerprint.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.361
Equator decides not to subscribe.

00:01:58.361 --> 00:02:04.800
Its data is deleted, including the four files
it uploaded, and the certificate records the

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.088
pack it took away.

00:02:06.088 --> 00:02:09.665
Inferiva made no determination, and filed
nothing.
